# function each(cb, n) { if (typeof n !== "number") return; for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) cb(i); }      sink(each);
# Where the code of `cb` lies is asked once in front of the loop, and each turn calls the answer at the site. For what is no function the answer is the stub that calls a value: it throws, and the error names what is called as it is written at the call:
# the words of the site hang on the address behind the call, also where the call goes through a register.
